# 04 - Button Press Counter

## Objective

Create a program using an ESP32 where every button press lights up a LED shortly as it is recorded and the total press times the button was pressed is displayed on the Serial monitor.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- LED
- 220 Ω resistor
- Push button
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- INPUT_PULLUP
- digitalWrite()
- if/else statements
- variables

## Wiring

- LED Anode → GPIO 21 (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- LED Cathode → GND 
- Push button pin 1 → GPIO 18
- Push button pin 2 → GND

## Expected Result

When the button is pressed, the LED lights up for 100ms and the buttonCounter will increment by 1. 

## What I Learned

- Serial Communication
- State Change Detection
- Variable states

